-- title:
--   Every character of the Hecke algebra is an eigenform
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $k$ an integer. Write $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ for the complex vector space of cusp forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$, and let $\mathrm{intLattice}$ denote the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ spanned by those cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers. Assume [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N k`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6), i.e. that the $\mathbb{C}$-span of this $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule is the whole of $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$, and assume $1 \le k$. Let $S$ be an arbitrary set of natural numbers and let [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N k S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\big(S_k(\Gamma_0(N))\big)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$. Then for every ring homomorphism $\chi$ from this Hecke algebra to $\mathbb{C}$ there exists a cusp form $f \in S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ with $f \neq 0$ such that $t f = \chi(t)\, f$ for every element $t$ of the Hecke algebra, the operator $t$ being taken through the inclusion into $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\big(S_k(\Gamma_0(N))\big)$.
--
--   This is one half of the dictionary between characters of a Hecke algebra and normalised eigenforms, in the form used by Deligne and Serre: a $\mathbb{C}$-valued character of the anemic Hecke algebra is realised by a simultaneous eigenvector in the space of cusp forms. It is the existence input for the construction of eigenforms with prescribed Hecke eigenvalues and for the passage from prime ideals of the Hecke algebra to eigenforms, and is cited by the statements producing normalised eigenforms with given $q$-expansion coefficients and by the occurrence of good eigensystems.
-- source:
